RF.put("questb:b12",{"8492":{"id":8492,"t":"The Alliance Needs Copper Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","obj":"Bring 20 Copper Bars to Sergeant Stonebrow at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Copper Bar","desc":"Hey there, ‹class›, you look fit enough to contribute to the war effort! We need all of the help that we can get here to put together the materiel needed for the Ahn'Qiraj War and it's your lucky day.\nI'm collecting copper bars in stacks of twenty. It's for a worthy cause, what do you say? Do you think you could help out the Alliance?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Have you collected those twenty bars of copper yet, trooper?","done":"You did it, lad! We'll get those copper bars onto the pile and put them to good use making the war materiel right away. It's the efforts of people like you that make me proud to serve the Alliance. Good work, soldier!\nAnd if you should happen to come across more copper bars, make sure that they find their way to me.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Sergeant Stonebrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"652":{"id":652,"t":"Breaking the Keystone","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and kill Fozruk. Bring the Rod of Order to the Keystone in the Arathi Highlands.\nRod of Order Fozruk","desc":"Opening the Stones of Binding loosened much of my confinement, but a lock still holds me chained. It is the Keystone you see among this circle of stones. And the key is held by one of my captors, the stone watcher Fozruk.\nYou must obtain that key, which the stone watchers call the Rod of Order, from Fozruk and use it to open the Keystone.\n‹name›, you have done so much to aid me. Just a little more...and my gratitude will shake the very foundations of the earth!","rew":"Experience: 3,450","back":"The Keystone is charged with tremendous geomantic energy.","done":"You place the rod in the keystone. And a shudder is felt beneath you...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":36.2,"y":57.4,"n":"Stone of Inner Binding","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":36.1,"y":58.1,"n":"Keystone","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"732":{"id":732,"t":"Tremors of the Earth","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Sign of the Earth for Garek.\nSign of the Earth Boss Tho'grun","desc":"I heard from Sigrun that you have been a great help to him. Perhaps I might enlist your help. I was sent here by my master, Krasus of the Kirin Tor, to put an end to the trouble brewing in Lethlor Ravine.\nI cannot divulge the exact nature of my assignment here or the tasks that I must undertake, but be assured it is of vital importance.\nA band of wandering ogres, sometimes seen near Camp Boff, stole an object called the Sign of the Earth; I must have it. Bring it to me, and I will tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The nomadic band of ogres travels between their camps across the Badlands; heat rising from the dry earth and the swirling winds will make it difficult to track their progress. I have heard that sometimes they travel through Camp Boff. If you are lost, you might try your search there.","done":"Good tidings you bring bearing the Sign, ‹name›. The Sign of the Earth was created by the Dark Iron dwarves of Angor Fortress to bind two of Deathwing's ruthless lieutenants, the twins Blacklash and Hematus.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":61.9,"y":54.3,"n":"Garek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97932":{"id":97932,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Uthan Stillwater in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.4,"y":60.6,"n":"Uthan Stillwater","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96652":{"id":96652,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the journal to Brakk near Razor Hill.\nProvided: Lost Journal","desc":"<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>","back":"Are you here to learn about camping in the wilderness?","done":"Is that my journal? I've been missing this for a while. Thank you, ‹class›.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Lost Journal","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94332":{"id":94332,"t":"Craftsmans writ arcanite skeleton key","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Arcanite Skeleton Key\nArcanite Skeleton Key","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Arcanite Skeleton Key, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Arcanite Skeleton Key Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94332","cats":["crafting"]},"94252":{"id":94252,"t":"Craftsmans writ red woolen boots","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Red Woolen Boots\nRed Woolen Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Red Woolen Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Yo!","done":"When I worked for the Venture Co, I had to wear these boots all day, every day. I thought I would be able to take these off and get comfortable in my own hut, but I didn't think of it until after I tracked mud everywhere.\nThese boots? They look way more comfortable. Second best thing to running around barefoot!","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7932":{"id":7932,"t":"12 Tickets - Lesser Darkmoon Prize","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Darkmoon Prize","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (12)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4812":{"id":4812,"t":"As Water Cascades","lv":14,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Empty Water Tube at the Auberdine moonwell, and then investigate the red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall.\nMoonwell Water Tube\nProvided: Empty Water Tube","desc":"Use this empty vial and fill up on some moonwell water here in Auberdine. Such potent magic should provide a clue as to the composition of the crystal. To do that, you'll pour the liquid over the crystal; it should take care of the rest.\nWhile I don't anticipate anything bad happening to you, I still want you to be careful. Above us to the east is Felwood; if that crystal is tied to that place as I suspect it is, then it could prove to be very dangerous.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The crystal looks very alien against the wooded scenery of Darkshore. You think you hear a very slight humming coming from deep within it.","done":"You have made it once more to the mysterious crystal. Removing the stopper on the tube of moonwell water, you gingerly pour the contents out over the top of the crystal. As the water cascades down its lattices, you see the opaque surface turn transparent...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":43.4,"n":"Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":47.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Mysterious Red Crystal","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4732":{"id":4732,"t":"Beached Sea Turtle","lv":19,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Turtle Remains Skeletal Sea Turtle\nProvided: Sea Turtle Remains","desc":"You find a corpse of a sea turtle that had beached itself on the coast of Darkshore some time ago. It has been picked nearly clean by Greymist murlocs, the very ones who now have encamped themselves around the creature's remains. Still, there appear to be some suitable samples left on the creature's remains that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine might be able to make use of.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 725\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings once again ‹name› - do you have any more discoveries to report to the Temple of the Moon?","done":"You've found even more beached creatures, ‹name›? Sea turtles were commonly found frolicking along the base of Nordrassil before it was destroyed. With the birth of Teldrassil, however, these creatures have been seen in ever decreasing numbers. Some, as we have discovered, end their lives here for some unknown reason.\nYour aid will perhaps unlock the mystery before us. Please accept this in exchange for the remains you have provided for our study.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":31.2,"y":85.6,"n":"Beached Sea Turtle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1052":{"id":1052,"t":"Down the Scarlet Path","lv":40,"min":34,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Brother Anton's Letter of Commendation to Raleigh the Devout in Southshore.\nLetter of Commendation\nProvided: Letter of Commendation","desc":"We of the Scarlet Crusade lay claim to strongholds from Hearthglen to Tirisfal Glades. We are quite proud of our bastions of cleansing throughout Lordaeron.\nYou have proven yourself against the undead in Desolace. But the true threat of the plague lies in Lordaeron.\nTravel to the town of Southshore, in the Eastern Kingdoms. Seek out a crusader named Raleigh the Devout. Give him this letter of commendation bearing my seal and he will escort you to a place of honor in our Scarlet Monastery.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Who goes there? What do you want from me?","done":"Brother Anton still spreads the word of the Scarlet Crusade? Oh my....\nDesolace Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.5,"y":7.9,"n":"Brother Anton","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Raleigh the Devout","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"92812":{"id":92812,"t":"Economic warfare","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"5 Carved Centaur Totem\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 92812","cats":["desolace"]},"5932":{"id":5932,"t":"Back to Thunder Bluff","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.","desc":"The time has come for us to part ways, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. Though the tauren are thought to be young in the ways of Cenarius, Turak Runetotem walks with much balance in the presence of nature. Listen to his instructions, and you will soon complete your first lessons into your role as a protector of balance.\nGo now, young one. We shall meet again.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Welcome back, ‹name›. I sense that your first meeting with the Great Bear Spirit is the same as it is with all druids when they first start down the path of the Claw... a little bewildering, but very intense. I know it was that way with me.\nThe Great Bear Spirit has been a part of Azeroth as long as Azeroth has existed in the heavens. We tauren listen closely to such spirits, and we all prosper from its purpose. Now, the time has now come for your first test of this purpose. Listen closely...\nMoonglade Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"9052":{"id":9052,"t":"Bloodpetal Poison","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 8 Bloodcap and 8 Gorishi Stings, and return to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.\n8 Gorishi Sting Gorishi Hive Queen , Gorishi Hive Guard 30 % , Gorishi Wasp 15 % , Gorishi Worker 15 % and 3 more\n8 Bloodcap Bloodpetal Sprout 50 %","desc":"I would ask you to help me create a toxin of sorts, to pacify a great creature living here in the crater. It is not deadly, and only the keen eyes of a ‹class› can hope to collect the ingredients.\nYou can find the bloodcap mushrooms growing within the bloodpetal sprouts all across the crater. Gorishi stings are from the insects inside and around the Slithering Scar, located in the southern part of the crater.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Major Healing Potion\nExperience: 5,100","back":"Have you met with success?","done":"The ingredients at last!\nWith the Un'Goro soil I have collected, the toxin is easily concocted...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"95212":{"id":95212,"t":"Never saddle on quality","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Pristine Leopard Pelts and deliver them to Amberstill Ranch.\n6 Pristine Leopard Pelt","desc":"We're getting ready to send a team of rams to reinforce the Alterac expedition, but we've run out of material to make their saddles.\nCollect pelts from the largest, fiercest leopards to the east and bring them to me. It's biting cold up there and our forces deserve nothing but the finest pelts to keep them warm!","back":"You look chilly, ‹class›. How goes the hunt?","done":"These pelts will make excellent saddles. You've done the Alliance proud, ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":49.8,"n":"Rudra Amberstill","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"412":{"id":412,"t":"Operation Recombobulation","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Razzle Sprysprocket in Kharanos 8 Restabilization Cogs and 8 Gyromechanic Gears.\n8 Restabilization Cog Leper Gnome 80 % , Gibblewilt 80 %\n8 Gyromechanic Gear Leper Gnome 80 % , Gibblewilt 80 %","desc":"Upon further analysis of the Gnomeregan situation, it would appear as though we not only failed to eradicate the troggs but we also happened to turn most of the gnomish race into horrific, mindless, evil-doing leper gnomes.\nOzzie and I plan to reverse the horrible leper effect with our latest invention: The Recombobulator. The machine is almost complete but we are in dire need of some Restabilization Cogs and Gyromechanic Gears. Retrieve some from the leper gnomes out front of Gnomeregan for us.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDriving Gloves Oil-stained Cloak\nExperience: 850\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The Recombobulator will be up and running as soon as we have sufficient Restabilization Cogs and Gyromechanic Gears.","done":"These Gyromechanic Gears and Restabilization Cogs are in perfect accordance with Ozzie's schematics for the Recombobulation Device. Once I add some hyrdolubricant to the inner combustion pistons, adjust the crank-o-ratchet and increase of the viscosity of the electrogum gel, the gnomish race will be as good as new.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":49.4,"n":"Razzle Sprysprocket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"812":{"id":812,"t":"Need for a Cure","lv":9,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar and get the Venomtail Antidote. Then bring the antidote to Rhinag near the northwestern border of Durotar.\nVenomtail Antidote","desc":"‹name›... your timing is perfect. I just hope I can compliment your haste as well.\nI was careless while fighting a few of the venomtails nearby, and one of them stung me deeply. I can feel its poison weakening me even as we speak. At this rate, I got maybe an hour left to live. But I'll need your help if I'm to do so...\nKor'ghan in Orgrimmar knows how to make the antidote. Find him... and hurry, ‹name›. I won't be able to last much longer. He should be in the Cleft of Shadow.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCharging Buckler Light Scorpid Armor\nExperience: 975\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I'm almost glad I can't return to Sen'jin as I am now. My weakness and stupidity would surely be mocked.","done":"‹name›, you've saved my life. Thank you.\nPlease take this; I hope it can at least help you in your travels, if not bring you some coin. From what you say, I won't be usin' it anytime soon. Kor'ghan is gonna march me through more of his rituals until I prove myself. More killin' boars, more gatherin' scorpid tails... <sigh>\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":41.5,"y":18.6,"n":"Rhinag","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"99052":{"id":99052,"t":"Threat from below","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill the sea giant along Durotar's north coast and bring back proof of your accomplishment.\nAggor's Belt","desc":"One of my scouts has reported a sea giant followed those naga down here. Not sure if they brought him intentionally or what, but he's dangerous in any case.\nIt's a young one, but it could still rip an orc in half in a heartbeat if they were caught off guard. I need him gone. But I'd suggest you find some help to deal with it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPristine Orcish Dagger Aggor's Refitted Belt\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Give 'em blood and thunder!","done":"Ha! I could hear his body fall from here!\nBe proud of your kill today, not many can claim they survived a fight with a sea giant.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"252":{"id":252,"t":"Translation to Ello","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Translated Letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke\nTranslated Letter\nProvided: Translated Letter","desc":"Oh my! If what is written on this note is true, then Abercrombie's done something...unspeakable.\nYou better bring the translated note back to Ello.\nAnd do so quickly, for I fear a doom already lumbers toward our town...","rew":"You will receive:\nTranslated Letter from The Embalmer\nExperience: 250","back":"Ah, is the note translated? Please, let me see it...","done":"<Ello reads the letter...and his face goes white. He then looks at you...>\nAlthough the aid you gave Abercrombie may have been motivated from kindness, your actions have doomed our town.\n<Ello becomes lost in his thoughts...>","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1372":{"id":1372,"t":"Nothing But The Truth","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Apothecary Faustin at Beggar's Haunt.","desc":"Our expeditionary force was sent at Varimathras's behest to survey lower Azeroth.\nWhile out scouting I noticed a human Infiltrator spying on Beggar's Haunt. Before I could apprehend him, some of our orcish... brethren... captured him and took him to Stonard, their stronghold in Swamp of Sorrows.\nI want to... help... our orcish allies. They did not see our camp here but nonetheless I want to lend a hand.\nWork with Faustin here to develop a... truth serum for our friend in Stonard.","rew":"Experience: 350\n+25 reputation with Undercity","done":"Zraedus was just telling me about the nosey little Infiltrator before you arrived.\nQuite a problem, indeed. The last thing we need is a busybody sniffing around Beggar's Haunt.\nI am sure the orcs of Stonard would be quite anxious to hear what our friend has to say. Seeing that they are our allies, ahem, we must help them to get any information they can from the human.\nWork with me, ‹name›, and we will deliver a truth serum to Stonard.\nFor the Horde!\n...did I get that right?","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.8,"y":35.6,"n":"Deathstalker Zraedus","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.5,"y":35.2,"n":"Apothecary Faustin","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9132":{"id":9132,"t":"Dark Iron Scraps","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Dark Iron Scraps Blackrock Raider 38.7 % , Blackrock Ambusher 35.3 % , Blackrock Battlemaster 35.2 % , Krom'Grul 34.9 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Dawn\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"For every armful of the scraps, I'll give you an insignia - the more the better. Now get out of my sight before I split you in two!","done":"That's all you brought me? Maybe you didn't hear me the first time. I need MORE!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91772":{"id":91772,"t":"Shhh were hunting kobolds","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Follow the kobold tracks and report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire with your findings and the Kobold Tracking Kit.\nFollowed Kobold Tracks : 0/ 6\nProvided: Kobold Tracking Kit","desc":"Alright. Take this kobold tracking kit. It'll let ye' track the kobold that Marshal McBride is concerned with.\nFollow the tracks and bring what ye' find to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\nI have a feelin' these varmints are up to somethin' outside Northshire. So ye'll be needin' Dughan's help.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 0 silver, 55 copper Experience: 270\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you figured out where the Kobolds are heading?","done":"What's this, Khalerenn? Tracking kobolds?\nWell, of course they're headed toward the Fargodeep mine! That place is infested with kobolds.\nGood work, I guess. I'm going to need someone to take care of that problem.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":51.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Tordrin Sternblade","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":65.8,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"95772":{"id":95772,"t":"Songblade search","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Look for Dorin Songblade's brother, Daewyn, in Whelgar's Excavation Site.","desc":"Me brother tried draggin' me off tae the Wetlands with some diggin' crew out o' Loch Modan. Said they were headin' into hills no dwarf's ever set boot in for some sort o' excavation.\nAye, I'd 'ave gone, if I wasn't already behind on this pile o' girdles I've got to refit.\nDaewyn normally writes after he sends off, though. Haven't heard a thing, gives me a strange feelin' this time.\nIf yer marchin' that way, mind checking in on me brother?","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":30.8,"y":46.6,"n":"Dorin Songblade","s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"2972":{"id":2972,"t":"Doling Justice","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Jer'kai's Signet Ring to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus.\nJer'kai's Signet Ring\nProvided: Jer'kai's Signet Ring","desc":"Out here in the wilderness, Kindal and I have meager means to reward your help, but we don't want you to feel unappreciated. Take my signet ring. If you ever find yourself in the boughs of Teldrassil, go to the Temple of the Moon in the heart of Darnassus. There you will find my High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. The ring will let her know that we are well and give credit to your story.\nWe both thank you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFirwillow Wristbands Nightscale Girdle\nExperience: 5,250\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, child. It pleases us to have more powerful adventurers here in the temple. If you have the time, will you share a tale or two with the younger adventurers? I know many of them would benefit from your wisdom.\nI'm sorry, look how rude of me. You've come to the Temple seeking our aid, and I impose on you. Please, forgive me. Tell me what the servants of the Light can do for you.","done":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›. It pleases us that you've not only helped dragonkind, but also one of our own priestess. Jer'kai was right to send you to me. I will make sure she has her ring returned to her--I have scouts heading the direction of Feralas soon. This will be one more thing for them to investigate while on their mission.\nThank you again, and please, make yourself at home while you're here.\nFeralas Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":65.9,"y":45.6,"n":"Jer'kai Moonweaver","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":81.6,"n":"Tyrande Whisperwind","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"9292":{"id":9292,"t":"Cracked Necrotic Crystal","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 60.","obj":"Bring the Cracked Necrotic Crystal to Lieutenant Orrin outside the gates of Stormwind.\nCracked Necrotic Crystal\nProvided: Cracked Necrotic Crystal","desc":"On the corpse of the fallen abomination, you discover a cracked crystal, slowly pulsing with necrotic energy.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Wizard Oil Consecrated Sharpening Stone","back":"Is there something you need?","done":"Hm, you took this from the corpse of one of the invading abominations?\nWe have received word about the necropolis base camps that are being summoned by the Scourge. I suspect they wanted to create one inside Stormwind. It is good that they were unseccessful.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69,"y":82.8,"n":"Lieutenant Orrin","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8652":{"id":8652,"t":"Graveborn the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":53.8,"n":"Elder Graveborn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8252":{"id":8252,"t":"The Siren's Coral","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Enchanted Coral and return them to Archmage Xylem.\n6 Enchanted Coral Spitelash Siren 80 %","desc":"Take a look around you. The ruins and beaches are overrun with spitelash. Recently, the wretched creatures have learned to recognize the rare components indigenous to Azshara.\nSpecifically, I speak of enchanted coral -- they are drawn to it by reasons unknown to me. Now there is little coral left in the bay, and it is vital to my research. I need you to separate some enchanted coral from the spitelash sirens and bring it to me.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"The spitelash sirens are surprisingly adept mages. Not as adept as you, I hope?","done":"This is a superb specimen of coral, ‹name›. Your skills are unquestionably precise and deadly.\nDo not think your efforts have gone unnoticed. Perhaps you are worthy of a true test of your skill...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"92":{"id":92,"t":"Redridge Goulash","lv":18,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Chef Breanna of Lakeshire wants five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.\n5 Great Goretusk Snout Bellygrub 37.9 % , Great Goretusk 36.4 %\n5 Tough Condor Meat Dire Condor 35.1 %\n5 Crisp Spider Meat Venom Mist Lurker 76.5 % , Giant Plains Creeper 53.6 % , Plains Creeper 50.6 % , Elder Moss Creeper 47.4 % and 4 more","desc":"Nothing would please me more than to make you some Redridge Goulash. But there's a slight problem. During the recent orc uprising I fed the entire brigade of Stormwind troops. My cupboard is now bare. But if you can provide me with the ingredients, I'd be happy to oblige.\nJust bring me five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Redridge Goulash Recipe: Redridge Goulash\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I still need five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. Such fine specimens too! And here is your delicious delicacy known as Redridge Goulash!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":17.6,"y":43.8,"n":"Chef Breanna","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8812":{"id":8812,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Ironforge.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":32.8,"n":"Gnomeregan Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":28.6,"n":"Officer Ironbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"97292":{"id":97292,"t":"Unending torment","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Inject the Hissing Serum into the system above Othmar's body for Master Apothecary Faranell.\nHissing Serum administered\nProvided: Hissing Serum","desc":"I have concocted a lovely serum that our new guest is sure to find quite... stimulating.\nTake this. Feed it into the workings dripping from above him. Let's see if we can't show him why it's in his best interest to serve loyally.\nAnd try not to drop it. I can't afford a new assistant.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650","back":"For Othmar's crimes against the Dark Lady, placing him under that oozing specimen is the least he deserves.\nAnd it's funny...","done":"Excellent. We'll let his flesh simmer for awhile. Give him time to acclimate to his new home.\nI have no further use for the wretch for now, but we shall keep an eye on him. I have many plans for Othmar's future.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.4,"y":69.4,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron"]},"3452":{"id":3452,"t":"The Flame's Casing","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return a Symbol of Ragnaros to Kalaran Windblade.\nSymbol of Ragnaros Twilight Idolater , Twilight Geomancer , Twilight Dark Shaman , Twilight Fire Guard","desc":"We need one final piece to form the torch.\nIn the mountains to the northwest you will find a large encampment of Twilight's Hammer. It is rumored that they carry symbols and idols that pay homage to their god. These symbols and idols could carry sufficient enchantment to form a magical casing. Bring me a single symbol of Ragnaros and I will try to extract the magic from the item to create the casing.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700","back":"Without a suitable source of arcane energy, the torch of retribution cannot be completed.","done":"The symbol radiates foul magic; perfectly suited for our task.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"3372":{"id":3372,"t":"Release Them","lv":52,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Mysterious Artifact being guarded by the Twilight's Hammer Idolaters in the northwest quadrant of the Searing Gorge and bring it to the Altar of Suntara in the Slag Pit.\nMysterious Artifact Twilight Artifact","desc":"Release them, ‹race›. Even after their bodies give out, the power of the Suntara forces them to complete their tasks.\nThe altar of Suntara is the key. Go northwest; in the hills above the cave... Twilight's Hammer guard a relic. Retrieve it and place it on the altar of Suntara.\n<The dying archaeologist collapses.>","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The altar is empty.","done":"You place the mysterious artifact on the altar of Suntara.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Dying Archaeologist","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41.3,"y":25.4,"n":"Altar of Suntara","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"972":{"id":972,"t":"Water Sapta","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Sapta","done":"Take the water sapta and find the corrupted pool of water in Silverpine, ‹name›. I have great faith in your abilities.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1532":{"id":1532,"t":"Call of Air","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.","desc":"The winds of Kalimdor rush to meet you and you shall be counted among some of our most powerful brothers/sisters. I am proud to see you have come this far and have such a promising future.\nThe element of air is a difficult one to control, but I have faith that your skills will overcome any obstacles that are placed in front of you.\nHead to the very south of the Barrens, and enter Thousand Needles. It is there, far to the east, that you will find Prate Cloudseer. She will teach you more.","rew":"You will receive:\nAir Totem\nExperience: 2,450","done":"For the time being. I shall give you what you need to focus your spells and to call upon the spirits of air. Take this totem, and when you are ready, train with me some more.\nThunder Bluff Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.2,"y":20.5,"n":"Xanis Flameweaver","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.5,"y":42.6,"n":"Prate Cloudseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8412":{"id":8412,"t":"Spirit Totem","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the pieces for the spirit totem to Bath'rah the Windwatcher.\n8 Bloodshot Spider Eye Carrion Vulture 20 % , Venom Mist Lurker 20 % , Carrion Lurker 2 % , Plague Lurker 2 %\n8 Thick Black Claw Carrion Vulture 20 % , Diseased Black Bear 20 % , Diseased Grizzly 2 %","desc":"The elemental spirits of this place don't be likin' me any more.\nYou know about the totems more than any, and I be needin' a spirit totem to protect me. We already got the elements, now we need somethin' more with more nature. More primal.\nIn the Western Plaguelands you can kill bears for claws and spiders for their eyes. The carrion birds eat everything, so they might have either one.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"The spirits know what we're up to, and they been tryin' to kill me! I hope you got the parts.","done":"Great, mon! Let's try it out...\nAlterac Mountains Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8332":{"id":8332,"t":"Dukes of the Council","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard and 3 Abyssal Crests to Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\nLarge Brilliant Shard\n3 Abyssal Crest Crimson Templar , Azure Templar , Hoary Templar , Earthen Templar","desc":"We think it is possible to use a wind stone to ambush a duke of the Abyssal Council. To do this, however, one must commune through the wind stone, and convince the council you are a middle ranked leader of the Twilight's Hammer.\nSuch a gambit requires a replica of the cult's medallion of station. I can create the medallion, but I will need a large brilliant shard, and crests worn by the Abyssal Templar.\nBring these to me and I will do the rest.","rew":"You will receive:\nTwilight Cultist Medallion of Station\nExperience: 6,600\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Do you have the shard and the crests, ‹name›? I will need them to make the twilight cultist's medallion of station.","done":"Ah, very good. I've been working on the medallion - now with these last ingredients, I'll be done in just a few moments...\nThere we are. Here is the medallion, ‹name›.\nYou'll need to wear this when you activate one of the Twilight's Hammer's wind stones. Put this on, along with the rest of the twilight trappings, and the Abyssal Council will see you as one of their cultist underlings.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8732":{"id":8732,"t":"Field Duty Papers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Prepared Field Duty Papers\nProvided: Signed Field Duty Papers","rew":"You will receive:\nSigned Field Duty Papers","back":"I take it you want those papers signed, boy/girl?","done":"Yes, I suppose that little skirmish will pass as field duty nowadays. Take these back to Cenarion Hold, I'm sure they'll have a cushy job ready for you.\nOff you go!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Krug Skullsplit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8572":{"id":8572,"t":"Veteran's Battlegear","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 Cenarion Combat Badges, 4 Cenarion Logistics Badges and 4 Cenarion Tactical Badges to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to be able to complete this quest.\n7 Cenarion Combat Badge\n4 Cenarion Logistics Badge\n4 Cenarion Tactical Badge\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The badges you collect from performing combat, logistics and tactical assignments for Cenarion Hold are more than just for show, ‹name›.\nYou'd be wise to hold on to them. As you prove your loyalty to our organization I can offer you some of the gear we reserve for our closest allies in exchange for those badges.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrace of Earth Band of Earthen Might Earthpower Vest\nExperience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"It's in our best interest to keep our most loyal allies well geared, ‹name›.","done":"Great work, ‹name›. Please accept this on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. You've certainly earned it, friend!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"172":{"id":172,"t":"Children's Week","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Orcish Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nProvided: Orcish Orphan Whistle","desc":"You're willing to help us here at the orphanage? Bless you, friend; your aid during Children's Week will be invaluable.\nTake this whistle. You will only be able to use it for a short amount of time - typically not longer than Children's Week itself. When you use it, you will be able to talk with the child you've agreed to look after. Using it again will dismiss the child.\nBy all means ‹name› - use the whistle and meet your ward! I'm sure the child will be most eager to meet you.","done":"Zug zug! My name is Grunth, and I guess you're looking after me? You're an adventurer, like my mom and dad were. My matron says that they died with honor in battle. I'm happy to meet you.\nI hope we'll do plenty of things together. I have some things I'd like to do, and the matron says you'll be like a big brother/sister to me during this week. I'd like that a whole bunch.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":70.7,"y":25.2,"n":"Orphan Matron Battlewail","s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"332":{"id":332,"t":"Wine Shop Advert","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Gallina Winery, and bring Suzetta Gallina the Wine Ticket for a free bottle of wine.\nWine Ticket\nProvided: Wine Ticket","desc":"If you talk to anyone about wine, then you know we Gallinas sell the best wine in Stormwind. And we're not far, still in the Trade District along the city's lovely canals.\nHere, take this pamphlet. Bring it to my sister Suzetta at our shop for a complimentary bottle of our famous pinot noir. You won't regret it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBottle of Dalaran Noir\nExperience: 130\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Greetings and welcome, master/madam. Have you yet tried one of our fine wines?","done":"Ah, so you've seen Renato? Well here you are, sir/ma'am. A bottle of our special pinot noir. You'll not find its equal in all of Azeroth!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":73.6,"n":"Renato Gallina","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.3,"y":76.8,"n":"Suzetta Gallina","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"572":{"id":572,"t":"Mok'thardin's Enchantment","lv":41,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Jungle Stalker Feathers to Far Seer Mok'thardin at the Grom'gol base camp.\n10 Jungle Stalker Feather Jungle Stalker 25 %","desc":"The items you gathered from the feline beasts of the Vale are only the first requirement for a powerful enchanted item. These jungle trinkets combined with my shamanistic ritual will provide you with a very useful tool in assisting the Horde and the Warchief.\nBut now you must gather for me some Jungle Stalker Feathers. The feathers are traditionally worn by the beasts on their armbands. You will find a tribe of the raptors directly south of Grom'gol, not far from the great arena.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did your gathering efforts prove fruitful?","done":"Most excellent. I will prepare these at once.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.1,"y":29.2,"n":"Far Seer Mok'thardin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5212":{"id":5212,"t":"The Flesh Does Not Lie","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover 10 Plagued Flesh Samples from Stratholme and return them to Betina Bigglezink. You suspect that any creature in Stratholme would have said flesh sample.\n10 Plagued Flesh Sample Shrieking Banshee 80 % in Stratholme , Venom Belcher 80 % in Stratholme , Bile Spewer 80 % in Stratholme , Patchwork Horror 80 % in Stratholme and 4 more","desc":"The Forsaken apothecaries are not the only beings in this world schooled in the sciences.\nI have been studying the plague for years, ‹race›. We had previously thought that the potency of the plague was dwindling, but what I have discovered here in the Plaguelands is startling. The plague seems to be growing in strength!\nI need to run more tests! The most potent source of the plague is from the tainted flesh of the most recently infected. Travel to Stratholme and bring me samples, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Some say I worry too much - to them I say, 'You don't worry enough!'","done":"There is something that has changed in the chemical structure of the plague's active agents. More data is required.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"892":{"id":892,"t":"The Missing Shipment","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Gazlowe's Ledger to Gazlowe in Ratchet.\nGazlowe's Ledger\nProvided: Gazlowe's Ledger","desc":"Everything looks square from my records, ‹name›. Go on back and tell Gazlowe he's out of luck. I wouldn't be surprised if it was the pirates that nabbed his goodies.\nNothing else I can do for him. Oh... though you could tell him that I've got some things from Undermine for him, when he has the time to come pick them up.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Ratchet","back":"So, what did Dizzywig have to say?","done":"No dice, eh? I guess it must have been the Freebooters then... Dizzywig's on the level, I'm sure he wouldn't cheat me like that. After all, he is on the payroll.\nLooks like I've got some goods to get back, ‹name›. What do you say?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5052":{"id":5052,"t":"Blood Shards of Agamaggan","lv":21,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Blood Shard to Mangletooth in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nCollect more Blood Shards if you want him to bless you with Agamaggan's power.\nBlood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","desc":"Along with the thorns, the blood affected <snort> other aspects of the earth: blood red stones mixed in with other minerals. The Bristleback dig up these shards and carry them as totems <snort> for strength in battle and as totems for their magics. <snort>\nI know the secrets of that magic.\nBring Mangletooth one of these blood shards to show you understand. Bring Mangletooth many of the shards, and he will bless you with quilboar magic--the magic of Agamaggan! <snort>","rew":"Experience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Our tribes flock to the thorny areas throughout the Barrens <snort> because they are holy places, but none as holy as Razorfen. Agamaggan's body makes up the entirety of the Razorfen, <snort> but the Downs are especially protected because the entrance is made from his great maw! <snort> It will swallow whole those not loyal to him, and spit out their bodies after he's chewed them up! <snort>\nAgamaggan has left his body behind to protect us, and he gives of his spirit so we may protect him. <snort>","done":"Ah, you do understand. <snort> My words were not lost on your ears, ‹race›. Mangletooth may be caged, but no cage can stop Agamaggan's power! <snort>\nThe touch of the shard, the feel of it... it has been a long time, ‹race›.\nDo you know what it is like? To have your power severed from you?\nBut, that is a tale for another time. I promised you information. I promised you Agamaggan's power. My people turned their backs on Mangletooth. Now, I lose you upon them. <snort>","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1452":{"id":1452,"t":"Rhapsody's Kalimdor Kocktail","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rhapsody Shindigger in The Hinterlands wants you to bring him 3 Roc Gizzards, 3 Groddoc Livers and 3 Ironfur Livers.\n3 Roc Gizzard Roc 75 % , Fire Roc 75 % , Searing Roc 75 %\n3 Ironfur Liver Ironfur Patriarch 75 % , Grizzled Ironfur Bear 75 % , Ironfur Bear 15 %\n3 Groddoc Liver Groddoc Ape 30 % , Groddoc Thunderer 30 %","desc":"Hiccup!\nSo that crazy fool Brohann sent ya? My we had quite an adventure...Hiccup!\nIf ya want me to tell ya what happened down in the swamp, I'm gonna need me something stiff to drink. It wasn't a pretty scene, ya see. Hiccup!\nTell ya what... bring me what I need to whip up a Kalimdor Kocktail and I'll tell ya all about it.\nGonna need some Roc gizzards from Tanaris... and let's see... some Groddoc and Ironfur livers from Feralas...\nA nice stiff Kalimdor Kocktail... that'll get me talking!","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Ya ever had a Rhapsody Malt? One of my finest brews, if I do say so myself. Hiccup!\nBut if I'm gonna relive the horrors of that fateful flight over... hiccup... the swamp, well I'm gonna need me something a wee bit stronger. Hiccup!\nDon't suppose you found me those gizzards and livers I need to add that extra kick to my Kalimdor Kocktail?\nHiccup!","done":"I see ya had no trouble at all getting me what I need! Musta been quite a stint you had over there in far-off Kalimdor.\nIt won't take but a moment for me to extract what I need from these gizzards and livers. Hiccup!\nThen I can distill me a fierce ol' drink and finally tell ya what ya wanna know.\nHiccup!\nGetting shivers just thinking about that ol' swamp.\nHiccup!\nLemme whip up a drink real fast.\nThe Hinterlands Tanaris Feralas","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.9,"y":48.6,"n":"Rhapsody Shindigger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"98252":{"id":98252,"t":"A void path","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Show Va'xug's Eye of Kilrogg the way back to the main Ashenvale road.\nEye of Kilrogg guided to the road","desc":"Show my Eye of Kilrogg the way out of this ravine and back to the Ashenvale road. Keep it moving and I'll follow once I see a clear path.\nI'll stay here--one of us should keep our bearings. If you lose the way, I can guide you back through the eye. I will not have us both wandering blind in this malicious forest.\nI can hold the channel for four minutes. No longer. Reach the road before the vision breaks, or return to me and we try again.\nLevel 22 , requires level 18 Difficulty 18 20 25 29 Side Horde Quest ID 98252\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 22, 3,050 XP in all.\n1 [ 22 ] Never Coming Back\nKill 6 Shadowhorn Stag and 6 Ashenvale Bear and return to Va'xug Firefure northwest of Fallen Sky Lake.\nVa'xug Firefure Ashenvale\n1,750 XP\n2 [ 22 ] A Void Path this quest\nShow Va'xug's Eye of Kilrogg the way back to the main Ashenvale road.\n1,300 XP","cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"492":{"id":492,"t":"A New Plague","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Johaan's Special Drink to the Captured Mountaineer.\nJohaan's Special Drink\nProvided: Johaan's Special Drink","desc":"According to the Deathguard, another one of those foolish Dwarven Mountaineers has just been captured. The Deathguard likes to use the cellar of the Gallows End Tavern as a holding cell until prisoners can be \"properly\" dealt with.\nWhy don't you go see how the Captured Mountaineer enjoys this special drink I made for him? It contains a subtle hint of what The Dark Lady has planned for the rest of Azeroth.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Why if I had my trusted rifle you'd be as good as dead, ‹class›. Just wait until the Steam Tank Brigade arrives to rescue me!","done":"Ah, a drink at last. I'm sure it's no Rhapsody Malt but I'll take anything to whet the old whistle at this point.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":51.4,"n":"Captured Mountaineer","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4492":{"id":4492,"t":"Lost!","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Ringo at Fire Plume Ridge.\nSpraggle's Canteen\nProvided: Spraggle's Canteen","desc":"You've got to help me, ‹name›! My friend, Ringo left earlier to explore the volcano to the south of here, and he has been gone way too long. I am really worried about him.\nDo you think you could find him? Why don't you take my canteen with you -- if you do find Ringo, I'm sure he'll need it!","rew":"Experience: 2,800","back":"Wha... What?","done":"Oh... I'm so glad someone found me...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.6,"y":8.5,"n":"Spraggle Frock","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":51.9,"y":49.8,"n":"Ringo","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1692":{"id":1692,"t":"Smith Mathiel","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Case of Elunite to Smith Mathiel.\nCase of Elunite\nProvided: Case of Elunite","desc":"I have placed the elunite you gathered into a case. Take it to the blacksmith Mathiel, and he will craft for you an elunite weapon.\nMathiel is to the south, on the other side of this building.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Greetings, young warrior. How might my skills serve you?","done":"Ah, elunite ore. This is a fine metal to work with, for it is blessed by the goddess Elune herself. It would be an honor to craft weapons with it.\nPlease wait while I work...","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":57.3,"y":34.6,"n":"Elanaria","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"4972":{"id":4972,"t":"Counting Out Time","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate 5 Andorhal Watches, found in lockboxes amongst the rubble of the city. Return with them to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.\n5 Andorhal Watch Small Lockbox","desc":"I need you to reach into the world beyond this room, ‹name›. Allow me to explain.\nYou see the difference in this room compared to the rest of Andorhal. My dragonflight works in many different ways and in many different timelines. To mend Andorhal's damage, I now act from a different timeline as not to overly contaminate it. To continue this though I need time trinkets, ones trapped from when the plague hit. Find them in lockboxes found in the ruined buildings that make up this once proud city.","rew":"You will receive:\nAttuned Dampener\nExperience: 5,800","back":"The time trinkets I seek are simple devices. They are watches mainly, and their hands are trapped forever when the plague first ravaged Andorhal.\nTime is never ending, and the watches you bring to me will invariably find themselves counted out back to their homes... that is, so long as the disturbances continue here.","done":"These are exactly what I need, ‹name›. Thank you.\nAllow me to suitably reward you with this. You may not understand what you would need with such a device. You might not even know quite what it really is. Alas, I cannot tell you when you will find it most useful; just know that at some point in the future, you may find this item to have extreme utility and function when consumed. Whether or not you choose to hold on to it until then... this, my friend, is up to you.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"12":{"id":12,"t":"The People's Militia","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to him on Sentinel Hill.\nDefias Trapper slain : 0/ 15\nDefias Smuggler slain : 0/ 15","desc":"The People's Militia has but one goal: To defend the lands of Westfall and return peace to our surroundings. Unfortunately, the price of peace is often blood.\nOne of my scouts has brought word of a band of Defias Trappers wreaking havoc nearby. I have reports of Defias Trapper sightings near the Jangolode Mine to the Northwest as well as at the Molsen Farm and Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm. If you seek to join our ranks, slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Perhaps I did not make myself clear, pledge. In order to prove your worth as a servant to The People's Militia and to the Light you need to slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me when the deed is done.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. My scout witnessed your valiant acts. You are proving yourself quite well so far.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"1132":{"id":1132,"t":"Fiora Longears","lv":20,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Fiora Longears on the docks at Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"Oh, to be at sea once again! To feel the kiss of the wind, and to have the waves rock me like my blessed mother, long ago!\nOh, I wish I had your fortune, good ‹class›, for I see the sea in your future!\nIt's my job to tell eager souls of the land of Kalimdor, the land of opportunity! If you're willing to try your luck across the sea, then take a ship from here to the lovely port of Theramore. Speak there with my partner, the elf, Fiora Longears.\nShe'll start you on your Kalimdor adventure!","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"Good day to you! You were sent by Mr. Flint in Menethil Harbor? Well Mr. Flint is a strong judge of character. If he sent you, then there's no doubt you belong here in Kalimdor!\nWetlands Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10,"y":58,"n":"Red Jack Flint","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.5,"y":45.1,"n":"Fiora Longears","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]}});